{title: Let it Snow}
{title-keyboard: Piano}

{columns: 2}

{capo-guitar: 5}
{key: C}
{transpose-keyboard: +5}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}

Oh, the [Cmaj7]weather out[Am7]side is [Dm7]frightful, [G]
But the [Dm7]fire is [D7]so de[G]lightful, [G/B]
And [Fmaj7]since we've [/E]no [/D]place [/C]to [G/B]go, [/E] [G]
Let it [G]snow, let it [G/B]snow, let it [Cmaj7]snow!

{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}

Well it [Cmaj7]doesn't show [Am7]signs of [Dm7]stopping, [G]
And I [Dm7]brought some [D7]corn for [G]popping; [G/B]
The [Fmaj7]lights are [/E]turned [/D]way [/C]down [G/B]low, [/E] [G]
Let it [G]snow, let it [G/B]snow, let it [Cmaj7]snow!

{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}

When we [G]finally [D]kiss good [G]night,
How I'll [Am7]hate going [D]out in the [G]storm;
But if [G]you really [D]hold me [G]tight,
[Em7]All the way [D7]home I'll be [G7]warm.

{end_of_chorus}

{column_break}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 3"}

The [Cmaj7]fire is [Am7]slowly [Dm7]dying, [G]
And, my [Dm7]dear, we're [D7]still good-[G]bye-ing, [G/B]
But as [Fmaj7]long as [/E]you [/D]love [/C]me [G/B]so, [/E] [G]
Let it [G]snow, let it [G/B]snow, let it [Cmaj7]snow!

{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}

When we [G]finally [D]kiss good [G]night,
How I'll [Am7]hate going [D]out in the [G]storm;
But if [G]you really [D]hold me [G]tight,
[Em7]All the way [D7]home I'll be [G7]warm.

